00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.750 align:start position:0%
 
now have a listen to this a staff member  at one of canada's biggest hockey teams  has thanked a fan who saved his life  after spotting a mole on the back of his  neck nadia popovich wrote notes on her  phone and signaled to brian hamilton to  read it and after seeing a doctor brian  hamilton confirmed the mole was in fact  cancerous and was later removed i'm  delighted to say that nadia joins us now  good to see you on sky news thank you  for your time today so you are being  regarded as a hero a heroine by many  uh yes it's it's still so much to wrap  my head around thank you so much for  having me it's this is surreal  now take us back what were you doing  there in the first place are you a big  hockey fan  oh huge yes i've grown up actually a fan  of the opposing team the canucks uh the  kraken is a brand new team in washington  state and in the states and uh this was  their very first home game against the  canucks  my old favorite team  uh and so i had to be there i was so  lucky that my my stepdad was able to  invite me and bring me into that seat  now take us back this was october the  23rd i believe so just over a couple of  months ago  and you were sitting there what did you  notice uh as far as mr hamilton's  concerns  yeah so uh he was a stranger at the time  he was actually located across from me  for the entire game so he wasn't even in  front of me for most of the game  but he happened to walk in front a  couple of times and during one of those  times he reached for something and the  lapel of his jacket fell down a little  and i was standing right behind him at  the time and i noticed a a dark spot and  it was a mole  so i was curious and i leaned up close  to the glass to take a a better look and  i noticed that you know it was  discolored it had irregular borders uh  it was pretty large and it was raised  and i knew those um just coming from a  little bit of a medical background that  those were possible indicators of skin  cancer and that he should likely be  seeing a doctor  goodness so i suppose you felt fairly  helpless did you and then  something  inspirational kicked in what did you do  yes yeah i i mean you can't speak  through the glass it's very hectic in  the arena  and so i thought you know if that was my  family member up there i would want  someone to say something and the only  way that i can say something is through  text through my phone so i pulled out my  notes app and i just quickly typed in  the mole on the back of your neck is  possibly cancerous please go see a  doctor  and i put mole cancer and doctor in  bright red and bolded font to see you  know if he only has one second to glance  at it maybe something will register and  the moment came together it was a  somewhat of a private moment and he was  able to read it i put my phone up to the  glass and knocked really loud uh and he  he took a look and uh  it was in the back of his mind and i'm  just so happy it turned out in the best  possible way could you see what his  reaction was when he managed to see your  notes  yes yeah so he he saw it and then he  kind of shrugged and and walked away  and after that moment i i kind of  regretted it i thought you know oh that  was inappropriate i shouldn't have  brought it up and maybe he already knows  about it and it's a sensitive topic and  so i just to not know for so many months  what happened to this man  and to finally put a name to the face  and and a story i mean it's it's been  incredible and and truly life-changing  so i suppose you didn't really know what  happened he saw this then went off and  this was in october we do know that he  he went to the doctor and got this  removed  but you perhaps wouldn't know that would  you because you hadn't been in contact  for a while  right i knew absolutely nothing until  just two nights ago when the story  dropped on social media and twitter had  a manhunt for me and  i mean i remember waking up that day to  my mom's phone call and she's screaming  and she says  nadia you have no idea what's going on  right now  and i i opened the the kraken team's  twitter  and there's red's story and he is  explaining how he he got it diagnosed  and removed and he's now cancer free and  all of this was happening and i had no  idea and  i mean  it's just so amazing to see how the  internet pulled together and and how  many people have been inspired by the  story to you know not only in in a  healthcare way to check themselves but  you know inspired by the unity between  the kraken and the canucks uh teams  uh it's not just while you're there let  us look at the moment that you did meet  brian red hamilton just a couple of days  ago  hi  hello hi it's so nice to me are you okay  with shaking hands  [Music]  thank you  what was that like to actually uh get to  see him and realize he'd done so much  good  yeah oh my goodness i mean  being able to hear from his mouth this  the story of what it was like on the  other side of the glass you know the the  confusion and the fear and  going home to his partner and saying do  i even have a mole on the back of my  neck um he he didn't even know it was  there let alone you know cancerous and  just to know that i was i was the  catalyst for that um is absolutely i  mean  i still can't believe it and now i mean  i've been able to speak to his family  while while i met him over face time and  i mean we're connected uh on social  media and i i just feel like this has  brought me and and his families together  forever and i i mean i'll i'll never  forget him  of course and a happy new year for you  and him and uh what have people done to  help you and your uh progression through  medical school  yes yeah so uh at the the game that i  attended where i got to meet red they  announced on the you know big booming  mic to the whole arena that they came  together as two teams and were giving me  a ten thousand dollar scholarship  and i almost fell back i  can't believe it even to this day i mean  i sat in my seat afterwards they  announced it and i i cried for like 10  or 15 minutes because  i mean really that money is is  it means so much to me and the  generosity  how many people have gone out of their  way to to welcome me and to tell me  their stories i mean  this scholarship is going to be applied  directly back into my medical education  and i'm just hoping i can have so many  more interactions just like the one i  had with red um in a doctor's office  this time  brilliant well even more they're amazing  because you did this in october it all  went away and you thought you'd hear  nothing more about it  right exactly yes i thought it was over  and it was just going to be a story in  my head that was a little bit awkward  but  i mean truly one amazing story  nadia well done and uh thank you very  much indeed for telling us your story  great to see you  thank you

